428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (A framework was developed to categorize synthetic data purposes, including: structural datasets for software testing, public-use files for educational purposes, scientific use files for research, realistic "twins" for analysis and ML and secure microdata sharing aligned with privacy expectations. Several methods explored about synthetic data generation, including statistical, rule-based, and machine learning methods like Generative Adversarial Networks \(GANs\). It also assessed privacy-preserving frameworks such as Differential Privacy and methods like Synthpop. The group also began categorizing privacy risk assessment methods, including attack models and risk metrics. In the next months, WP13 plans to finalize synthetic data methodologies, map statistical domains to methods, and run proof-of-concept experiments, ensuring research based on data's privacy without compromising its utility.)
/E (A framework was developed to categorize synthetic data purposes, including: structural datasets for software testing, public-use files for educational purposes, scientific use files for research, realistic "twins" for analysis and ML and secure microdata sharing aligned with privacy expectations. Several methods explored about synthetic data generation, including statistical, rule-based, and machine learning methods like Generative Adversarial Networks \(GANs\). It also assessed privacy-preserving frameworks such as Differential Privacy and methods like Synthpop. The group also began categorizing privacy risk assessment methods, including attack models and risk metrics. In the next months, WP13 plans to finalize synthetic data methodologies, map statistical domains to methods, and run proof-of-concept experiments, ensuring research based on data's privacy without compromising its utility.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
